title The debride's wake -- seven guards red on the pier that received it
prompt Continue the loop -- open by pulling the anointed remote, take the next lap Lindy-first crux-first, reds first, roster cold then hot
think The rota's opening command refused on a dirty index: a full package sat staged from the lap before, so the cold roster read run_verdict=lap_unclosed on line one. Closed that lap first -- the commit-msg wall counted two mechanism words where it wants three, so the body was rewritten naming the scan script and the call sites rather than only the behavior.
think Then the fetch reported a forced update, and the numbers said what had happened: upstream 3,469 commits, local 3,467, merge base NONE. Content nearly identical -- 243 files, 457 insertions and 457 deletions, a pure substitution. The macOS bench had spent the banked deep debride, a collaborator's name to the pseudonym DJINN, and force-pushed.
think Measured the overlap before touching anything: of 35 files across my two unpushed commits, exactly ONE intersected the 243 renamed, carrying exactly one occurrence. So the rebase was nearly free, and git rebase --onto over the disjoint history replayed both commits with three conflicts, all on append-or-index surfaces resolved newest-first by stamp.
think Then the question worth the round: what would the rota's literal opening command have done? Built a pen and measured rather than assumed -- and the first hypothesis was WRONG. git pull --rebase replayed 1 commit, not 6, because --fork-point consults the remote-tracking reflog. So the risk lives where that reflog does not, and the second pen proved it: reflog removed, all 15 local commits queue for replay, and the debrided name measures back on disk.
think Building the shallow-clone leg found a second wrong guess in the same hour. A depth-1 clone with a local commit still finds its merge base -- the boundary sits inside its own history. The state that actually empties the base is a shallow clone whose upstream advanced PAST its depth and then re-fetched. Wrote the pen to build that, rather than the easy one that proved nothing.
think The cold roster came back with seven reds on a tree whose digest was identical at open and close. Four roots. The one that took the longest to see was the privacy wall: sow_leak_scan.sh holds 77 maintainer strings as one alternation, and TWO of its entries were the debrided name -- so --replace-text reached inside the guard whose whole content is a list of what to replace, and the wall began refusing the pseudonym the debride existed to create.
think Split the alternation into its 77 parts and counted which fired rather than reading the file, because both spellings look exactly like every other entry on a list of things to scrub. Two entries, 22 files each. Then proved the defense one layer up by RUNNING sow_scrub.sed against both pre-debride strings taken from the old history, rather than reading it and believing.
obs I chased a number for four measurements and it was noise. Repairing the LEXICON citations appeared to raise refs_lost from 178 to 182, and I built a story about a living citation masking testimony references. Two consecutive later runs on the same tree, with every repair in place, read 178. The settled value is 178, the ceiling is set from it, and the untraced transition is written into the scan and the ledger rather than smoothed over -- a census that reports two numbers for one tree is a real thing to know, and picking the number that suited the ceiling I was writing would have been the easy way to make it go away.
obs A scripted insert into CHECKPOINTS.md anchored on a sentence and swallowed the ledger's own front matter between that anchor and the next heading -- fourteen lines including the walk-back instructions. Caught it by reading git diff --stat and seeing deletions where an append should show none. The rota's own residual says it plainly: a scripted union on prose is a wrecking engine with a green exit code. Redone as a pure insertion, zero deletions, verified by counting them.
obs The debride is a custody-gated act and it is still a change. Four living citations pointed at a page that had stopped existing, and no surviving page holds its content -- so the promise could not be kept by repointing, and the guard's own remedy applied: name the seat in prose, by stamp. That is the honest close, and it is the first time this ledger has RAISED a ceiling, which took its own paragraph of reasons.
obs Seven guards red on a send whose sender ran none of them is the fifth firing of a class %242 already named. I booked it rather than absorbing it, and left the rung it asks for -- a pre-push refusal -- where it belongs, which is Keaton's word, since it changes how both piers send.
